      { q:"What confession does Hosea 14 put in returning Israel's mouth?", choices:["Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses; the work of our hands is not our god","We have kept your statutes from our youth","Judah alone is guilty","Baal and the Lord are one"], a:0, why:"Verses 3-4 script the renunciation of Assyria, horses, and idols, resting on the God in whom the fatherless findeth mercy." },
      { q:"What does the Lord being as the dew unto Israel promise?", choices:["Constant fog over the mountains","Quiet, renewed grace that makes the penitent grow as the lily and root as Lebanon","A change of climate","That dew replaces rain"], a:1, why:"I will be as the dew unto Israel: he shall grow as the lily, and cast forth his roots as Lebanon." }
